3,1,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Minako,,"Since our informal arrangement is breaking down, we need a structured system. To ensure fairness, we should first clarify the actual costs and usage patterns. I suggest we look into the data before deciding on a new rule.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree, Minako. A bit of empirical data would certainly prevent us from relying on mere impressions. Let's ensure our new system is based on logic rather than frustration.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. However, fairness isn't just about money. We need to address the actual reliability of the car's availability and its condition when we need it. Data on usage patterns will be essential for that.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. We've been operating on guesswork for too long. If we want a logical system, we need the real figures first. I want to see exactly who has been driving and what the actual costs are.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. It's been a bit stressful lately, hasn't it? I think it's a good idea to look at the data so we don't have to argue about it anymore.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minako,,"To get a clear picture of an even split, I will look into last year's tax, insurance and parking papers, as well as last year's fuel receipts. These will establish our baseline financial obligations.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"To ensure we don't overlook the human element, I'll examine what two other car-sharing households said and the hours of use recorded in the diary. It's wise to see how others avoid these frictions.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Asuka,,I will look into the state of the car at handover and the mechanic's remarks at the last service. We need to know if the vehicle is being maintained properly for the next person.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shion,,"I'll take the month's trial of recording every run and the spell of checking each other's figures. If we want an honest picture of usage and costs, we need precise, verified data.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,I'll... look into the trips that repeat weekly and the weeks of heavy use over the year. I want to see if there are patterns that make the scheduling so difficult.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minako,,"It seems we have a comprehensive plan. By dividing these tasks, we can cover the financial, mechanical, and behavioral aspects of our sharing arrangement without duplicating effort. Does everyone feel comfortable with their assigned items?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems perfectly balanced. We have the accountants, the mechanics, and the sociologists all represented. I believe this approach will provide the clarity we need without turning the process into a trial.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"I am comfortable. However, let's remember that the goal isn't just to balance a ledger, but to ensure the car is actually usable and ready for whoever needs it next. Data should serve that purpose.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, usability is a result of a fair system. If the costs are skewed, someone will inevitably neglect the car. Let's focus on the hard numbers first; that's the only way to be truly objective.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope the numbers help. I just want us to find a way that doesn't feel so... overwhelming for everyone. I'm okay with the plan.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minako,,"Then it is settled. Let's proceed with our research. Once we have the facts, we can discuss how to distribute the costs and usage fairly. I look forward to seeing what we discover.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. Let us hope the findings illuminate a path toward a sustainable agreement. I shall await the results with a mixture of curiosity and cautious optimism. Until then, let's maintain our composure.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Asuka,,I'll be waiting for the results. Let's make sure we don't ignore the practical details of the car's condition once we have the data. I'm ready to move forward.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Shion,,I'm ready. Let's see if the reality matches our assumptions. I expect the data to reveal some significant gaps in how we've been handling things. I'll see you all in the next round.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll... do my best to find the patterns. I hope we can just find a way to make things simpler for everyone. See you all soon.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
