35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The financial data is revealing. Fixed costs are over 280,000 yen, but fuel contributions are heavily lopsided, with two people paying for most of it. We cannot maintain a fair system if some are quietly subsidizing others.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we've uncovered a classic imbalance. While the numbers are illuminating, I'm more concerned that we're focusing on the ledger. If we only fix the money, we might miss the underlying friction that actually erodes our harmony.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The financial imbalance is one thing, but the physical state of the car is another. I found that the vehicle is often left with rubbish inside and nearly empty on fuel. This makes the car unreliable for the next user.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's clear that our ""informal"" way was just a mask for inefficiency. My findings show that precise tracking is time-consuming and creates tension, but that's exactly why we need a logical, automated system rather than emotional guesswork.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that a lot of the stress comes from those weekly repeats and the sudden bursts of heavy use. It seems like we spend whole evenings just trying to coordinate everything, which is... really exhausting.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, harmony is built on fairness. If we ignore the fact that some are paying for others' fuel, resentment will only grow. We need a system that accounts for both fixed costs and actual usage to be truly sustainable.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, fairness is indeed the goal, but we must be careful not to mistake accounting for harmony. If we implement a system of constant auditing, we may find we've traded financial resentment for administrative exhaustion.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, I agree that auditing is exhausting, but neglecting the car is a different kind of burden. If the car is empty or dirty, the next person pays a time and stress tax. We need a standard for handover.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, a handover standard is just a rule; it doesn't solve the root cause. People neglect the car because they aren't financially invested in its upkeep. If we fix the payment logic, the behavior will follow.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Benjamin is right about the exhaustion. Even if we fix the money, the time we spend arguing and planning every single trip is just... too much. Can't we find a way to make it simpler?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, simplicity is a goal, but not at the cost of equity. If we simply ignore the fuel disparity, we are choosing a ""simple"" system that is fundamentally unfair to those who have been paying more.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, I am not suggesting we ignore the disparity, but rather that we avoid a solution that requires us to act as each other's accountants. Constant verification is a recipe for resentment, not resolution.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, I disagree. Financial investment doesn't automatically lead to cleanliness or consideration. A person can pay their share and still leave rubbish behind. We need a system that prioritizes the car's readiness for the next user.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, you're focusing on symptoms. The ""rubbish"" and ""empty tanks"" are results of a lack of accountability. When payments are vague, responsibility becomes vague. A precise, logical payment structure creates the necessary ownership to ensure the car is respected.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just feel like we're talking about rules and money, but the actual act of organizing is what's wearing me down. If the new system is too complex, won't we just spend more time arguing?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We must find a balance. A system that is too simple is unfair, but one that is too complex is unsustainable. Let's look at the proposed options and choose the one that ensures equity without creating an administrative burden.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. Let us hope the options provide a middle ground. I would strongly caution against any proposal that mandates constant auditing; we should aim for a system that restores our friendship, not one that turns us into debt collectors.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. However, we must ensure the chosen option includes a clear, enforceable standard for the car's condition. A ""simple"" system that allows the car to remain a mess is not a solution; it's just deferred stress.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your fear of ""debt collecting"" is just a preference for ambiguity. I'm not interested in friendship if it's based on someone else subsidizing my life. We need a system where the numbers are indisputable and the logic is cold.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I don't want us to fight. I just hope the options have something that doesn't require so much talking and planning. I'm really looking forward to a way that's just... easier for everyone.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
